sec.p:
The model for each channel consisted of five closed (C) and one open (O) state. The transition between the first five steps was voltage dependent and the last step voltage independent:
(2)
C0⇄α1(V)β1(V)C1⇄α2(V)β2(V)C2⇄α3(V)β3(V)C3⇄α4(V)β4(V)C4⇄ab0 \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} C_{0} \underset{\beta_{1}(V)}{\stackrel{\alpha_{1}(V)}{\rightleftarrows}} C_{1} \underset{\beta_{2}(V)}{\stackrel{\alpha_{2}(V)}{\rightleftarrows}} C_{2} \underset{\beta_{3}(V)}{\stackrel{\alpha_{3}(V)}{\rightleftarrows}} C_{3} \underset{\beta_{4}(V)}{\stackrel{\alpha_{4}(V)}{\rightleftarrows}} C_{4} \underset{b}{\stackrel{a}{\rightleftarrows}} 0 \tag{2} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
a and b are the rate constants for transitions between C4 and O, and αi(V) and βi(V) are the voltage dependent forward and backward transition rates that are given by:
(3a)
αi(V)=αi,0exp⁡(V/ki)i=1−4 \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \alpha_{i}(V)=\alpha_{i, 0} \exp \left(V / k_{i}\right) \quad \mathrm{i}=1-4 \tag{3a} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
(3b)
βi(V)=βi,0exp⁡(−V/ki)i=1−4 \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \beta_{i}(V)=\beta_{i, 0} \exp \left(-V / k_{i}\right) \quad \mathrm{i}=1-4 \tag{3b} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
where αi,0 and βi,0 are the forward and backward rate constants at 0 mV and ki a slope factor.

Ca2+ binding to all buffers (B) was simulated by second order kinetics with forward and backward binding rate constants kon and koff, respectively:
(4a)
d[Ca]dt=−kon[Ca][B]+koff[CaB] \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d[C a]}{d t}=-k_{o n}[C a][B]+k_{o f f}[C a B] \tag{4a} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
(4b)
d[B]dt=−d[CaB]dt \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d[B]}{d t}=-\frac{d[C a B]}{d t} \tag{4b} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
Diffusion of all species (X) was simulated according to
(5)
d[X]dt=DxAn,n±1Vnr([X]n±1−[X]n) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \frac{d[X]}{d t}=D_{x} \frac{A_{n, n \pm 1}}{V_{n} r}\left([X]_{n \pm 1}-[X]_{n}\right) \tag{5} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
where DX is the diffusion coefficient, A the surface, V the volume and r the radius of a shell (n). Ca2+ was cleared by a linear, surface-based extrusion mechanism driven by the difference between [Ca2+]i and the resting [Ca2+]i (30 nM according to the imaging data).
